worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_meta_reasoner.js"
  ceiling 1197
  rationale "The recursive meta reasoner (2026-10-06 meta-algorithm doctrine), JavaScript first: opens every request word as an unknown, grounds it from request definitions, learned chunks, instruction-set documentation and dictionary captures (recursing into glosses), plans, and keeps a links-notation derivation. Domain-free; its vocabulary, instruction set and response templates are data/seed/meta-reasoning.lino. New capability with no native counterpart yet; Rust follows by translation. Ceiling moved 864 to 953 for universal quantifiers, the bound's unit naming a measure, prose-embedded examples, effect-free measures and the seeded trace wording (note records). Ceiling moved 953 to 1175 for location operands after a file noun, imperatives that name an operation, symbols a gloss quotes as request values, the superlative degree grounding its stem as a measure, interrogatives never read as defined terms, and seeded degree, selector, filter-measure and takes records. Ceiling moved 1175 to 1197: metaIsFileNoun is factored out of metaLocationOperands and metaNamesFileNoun added, the twins of is_file_noun / names_file_noun in rust/src/meta_reasoner/request.rs that the write_script route consults."
